      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.34.0"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## HOW TO: Wan 2.2 14B First-Last Frame (Fast 4-Step LightX2V)\n\n### 1. Speed vs Quality\n- Runs in **4 total steps** (2 High-Noise + 2 Low-Noise, CFG `1.0`, Shift `5.0`) \u2014 very fast on a 3090!\n- Want cleaner hands/motion? Use **`Wan2.2_14B_I2V_FLF_8StepOrBase20Step.json`** (8-step LoRA or full 20-step base).\n\n### 2. How to change LENGTH & RESOLUTION\n- **Duration:** Edit `Duration in seconds` (Group 2). Wan 2.2 runs natively at **16 fps** and snaps to `4n + 1` frames (`3s=49`, `4s=65`, **`5s=81`**, `6s=97`). Stay at 5s or less for best coherence.\n- **Resolution (must be \u00f7 16):**\n  - 16:9 fast: **`832\u00d7480`** (default) | higher detail: `960\u00d7544` or `1280\u00d7720` (heavy on 24 GB)\n  - 9:16 vertical: `480\u00d7832` | 1:1 square: `640\u00d7640` or `768\u00d7768`\n- **1-Image I2V only:** Disconnect `end_image` on `WanFirstLastFrameToVideo`.\n\n### 3. How to Add Audio to Wan 2.2\nWan 2.2 generates **video only** (no native audio). Three easy options:\n1. **Mux music/SFX/voiceover right here:** Select `LoadAudio` + `TrimAudioDuration` -> **Ctrl+B**, pick your WAV/MP3, and it trims & muxes into the MP4 automatically!\n2. **AI-generated SFX/Foley:** Run **`ComfyUI-MMAudio`** on the saved MP4 to generate synchronized sound effects from the video frames (~5 GB VRAM, seconds on 3090).\n3. **DaVinci Resolve / Talking shots:** Score and mix in DaVinci Resolve \u2014 or use **LTX-2.5** / **MiniMax H3** for shots where characters speak on camera.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## HOW TO: Wan 2.2 14B First-Last Frame (Fast 4-Step LightX2V)\n\n### 1. Speed vs Quality\n- Runs in **4 total steps** (2 High-Noise + 2 Low-Noise, CFG `1.0`, Shift `5.0`) \u2014 very fast on a 3090!\n- Want cleaner hands/motion? Use **`Wan2.2_14B_I2V_FLF_8StepOrBase20Step.json`** (8-step LoRA or full 20-step base).\n\n### 2. How to change LENGTH & RESOLUTION\n- **Duration:** Edit `Duration in seconds` (Group 2). Wan 2.2 runs natively at **16 fps** and snaps to `4n + 1` frames (`3s=49`, `4s=65`, **`5s=81`**, `6s=97`). Stay at 5s or less for best coherence.\n- **Resolution (must be \u00f7 16):**\n  - 16:9 fast: **`832\u00d7480`** (default) | higher detail: `960\u00d7544` or `1280\u00d7720` (heavy on 24 GB)\n  - 9:16 vertical: `480\u00d7832` | 1:1 square: `640\u00d7640` or `768\u00d7768`\n- **1-Image I2V only:** Disconnect `end_image` on `WanFirstLastFrameToVideo`.\n\n### 3. How to Add Audio to Wan 2.2\nWan 2.2 generates **video only** (no native audio). Three easy options:\n1. **Mux music/SFX/voiceover right here:** Select `LoadAudio` + `TrimAudioDuration` -> **Ctrl+B**, pick your WAV/MP3, and it trims & muxes into the MP4 automatically!\n2. **AI-generated SFX/Foley:** Run **`ComfyUI-MMAudio`** on the saved MP4 to generate synchronized sound effects from the video frames (~5 GB VRAM, seconds on 3090).\n3. **DaVinci Resolve / Talking shots:** Score and mix in DaVinci Resolve \u2014 or use **LTX-2.5** / **MiniMax H3** for shots where characters speak on camera.\n"
      },
      "title": "HOW TO: Length, Resolution & Audio (Wan 2.2 4-Step)",
      "color": "#233",
      "bgcolor": "#355"
    },
